  "architecture_name": "[mobilenet_v3_small] mobilenet_v3_small_adapter",
  "architecture_family": "mobilenet_v3_small",
  "description": "A lightweight MobileNetV3Small backbone adapted to a single\u2011channel 5\u2011second mel\u2011spectrogram, using a 3\u00d73 conv to handle the 1\u2011channel input, ending with a dropout\u2011regularized dense head; the image is resized to 112\u00d7112 for faster GPU/CPU inference.",
  "reasoning": "Prior custom CNN experiments failed due to CUDA/Numpy gradient usage, so we avoid custom ops. MobileNetV3Small offers a proven, low\u2011memory backbone (~2\u202fM parameters) that fits within the 90\u2011minute runtime budget, and its inference can be CPU\u2011only. SpecAugment (horizontal flip, vertical flip, time\u2011shift) improves robustness for minority classes without increasing memory. Resizing to 112\u00d7112 rather than 224\u00d7224 reduces compute, eliminating the risk of runtime overload. This configuration is DP\u2011safe, stable, and likely to outperform the less\u2011reliable custom CNN for the long\u2011tail multi\u2011label classification task."
}

