{
  "architecture_name": "[custom_cnn] cnn_small_v2",
  "architecture_family": "custom_cnn",
  "description": "A lightweight CNN with three 3x3 convolutional blocks, batch normalization, adaptive average pooling, and a softmax head for multi-label bird species classification.",
  "reasoning": "The custom CNN avoids prior failures by not using transfer learning or complex attention (like EfficientNet or MobileNet). It maintains a ~800k parameter count, fits comfortably in CPU memory, and uses only stable operations. Concrete details: 3\u00d73 Conv2d blocks with incremental channel expansion, BatchNorm, 0.2 dropout after the final conv, SpecAugment (horizontal flip, 90\u00b0 rotation), MixUp 0.2 with label smoothing, and a 206\u2011unit softmax head. Risk: potential over\u2011fitting due to high class count; mitigation: early stopping on validation loss, data\u2011level augmentation, and label smoothing reduce label noise."
}
